 <frangarcj@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 16:58:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv: bail out of the whole batch
 on illegal first draw
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The batch reuses the first draw's setup (vertex program patch, streams,
textures) for every subsequent sceGxmDraw. If that setup failed, the
per-call path would simply skip the one draw and revalidate on the next
call — but the batch loop would keep issuing sceGxmDraw against invalid
state. Return early instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/custom_shaders.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/custom_shaders.c b/source/custom_shaders.c
index 5c7bdeb..55fd6ef 100644
--- a/source/custom_shaders.c
+++ b/source/custom_shaders.c
@@ -3172,7 +3172,12 @@ void vglMultiDrawElementsUniform4fv(GLenum mode, GLint uniform_location,
 	GLboolean is_draw_legal = _glDrawElements_CustomShadersIMPL(src, count, top_idx, 0, SCE_GXM_INDEX_SOURCE_INDEX_16BIT);
 
 #ifndef SKIP_ERROR_HANDLING
-	if (is_draw_legal)
+	// Unlike glDrawElements, the batch reuses the first draw's setup for every
+	// subsequent sceGxmDraw — if that setup failed, none of the draws may run.
+	if (!is_draw_legal) {
+		restore_polygon_mode(gxm_p);
+		return;
+	}
 #endif
 	{
 		// setup_elements_indices(uint16_t) inlined for the mode==GL_TRIANGLES /
